<title>UK: EIB sets C$100 million six-year bond.</title>
<headline>EIB sets C$100 million six-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Toronto-Dominion Bank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    C$100 MLN     COUPON     5.75	MATURITY    30.DEC.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.47    PAY DATE  L-29.NOV.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    99.87     SPREAD	+15 BP</p>
<p> NOTES    L-LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/CA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    LONDON    HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.275     SELL CONC  1.60	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>		 UNSECURED, UNSUBORDINATED.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
